    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11367-026-02634-z",
    "abstract": "The topic of dynamic LCA has received quite some attention since 2010. Especially dynamic characterization factors for assessing the climate impact of greenhouse gases have become more mainstream. Here we review the principles of these approaches. The seminal paper by Levasseur and co-authors from 2010 is analyzed in depth, along with several follow-up papers by a variety of authors. The emphasis in our analysis is on the modelling details and in some cases the numerical outcomes and the units. All papers that are analyzed contain unclear parts and possible mistakes. They also misquote the original proposal in several cases. We consider this as a potential threat to the scientific status of dynamic LCA and, by extension, to the scientific status of LCA. We provide several fixes in the modelling details. We also propose a way forward to better understand and communicate the principles of dynamic LCA.",
    "field": "Dynamic Life Cycle Assessment",
    "problem": "Papers proposing and applying dynamic characterization factors in Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) contain unclear parts, possible mistakes, and misquotations, which threatens the scientific status and credibility of the dynamic LCA methodology.",
    "method": "This paper critically reviews dynamic characterization methods, identifies unclear parts and mistakes in the modeling details of seminal papers, and proposes several fixes to the mathematical formulas and notational principles to better understand and communicate the principles of dynamic life cycle assessment.",
    "task": "The task is to critically review the methodological principles of dynamic characterization factors for assessing climate impact in Life Cycle Assessment, analyzing seminal and follow-up papers to identify and correct modeling inconsistencies, unclear parts, and mistakes.",
